      "message": "PS1 -\u003e PS2 includes the fix for a subtle bug that was found by some bots.\n\nMCRec used to rely on never being copied or moved (because SkDeque makes that guarantee). The \"construct a rec on top of another one\" had a signature that made it look like a copy-constructor, even though it had totally different semantics. SkSTArray does need to move these things now (when re-allocating), so I added an explicit move constructor, and changed the signature on the other constructor to not be accidentally usable as a copy-constructor.",
